15. CREATE AUTOMATED TESTS
==========================

Implement unit tests, integration tests, and realistic end-to-end scenarios.

At minimum, test the following cases.

TEST A: C+ STUDENT

A student with a C+ mean grade must be evaluated against every degree programme in the database for which C+ is sufficient and whose subject prerequisites they satisfy.

The engine must not return only computing, business, or other predefined popular courses.

TEST B: B- STUDENT

A student with B- must be evaluated across all relevant fields and qualification levels.

The engine must not assume that a stronger mean grade makes every subject prerequisite valid.

TEST C: B+ STUDENT

A student with B+ must receive comprehensive matching across all fields.

A high mean grade must not hide eligible programmes outside the student's selected career interest.

TEST D: A STUDENT

A student with A must receive the same comprehensive evaluation, with eligibility determined by the actual subject requirements.

TEST E: STRONG MEAN GRADE, WEAK REQUIRED SUBJECT

A student with B+ but below the required Mathematics grade for a specific engineering programme must not be marked eligible for that programme if the prerequisite is verified.

Other programmes for which the student qualifies must still be returned.

TEST F: MISSING SUBJECT GRADE

If a required subject grade is missing, the engine must not silently assume the student passed it.

Return an appropriate incomplete-data or verification status.

TEST G: MULTIPLE CAREER INTERESTS

A student interested in medicine must still be able to discover all other academically qualifying fields.

TEST H: PROGRAMME RESULT COUNT

If 200 programmes satisfy the eligibility conditions, the engine must retain all 200 in the complete results even when the first page displays only 20.

TEST I: CLUSTER SCORE CONSISTENCY

The same programme must display the same correctly calculated score in its card, report summary, PDF, and counselor input.

TEST J: OUTDATED CUT-OFF

An older historical cut-off must never be presented as a confirmed current-year admission requirement.

TEST K: UNKNOWN PROGRAMME REQUIREMENTS

A programme with incomplete official requirements must not be falsely classified as confirmed eligible or confirmed ineligible.

TEST L: TVET ELIGIBILITY

Students must be evaluated against the relevant diploma, certificate, artisan, and other TVET entry criteria without incorrectly applying university degree cluster-point rules.

TEST M: INSTITUTION VALIDATION

An institution must not be shown as offering a programme unless that relationship is supported by the programme database.

TEST N: EMPTY OR INVALID DATA

The system must handle invalid grades, missing subjects, incomplete datasets, and zero matching programmes gracefully.

Use real official programme data where available and synthetic student records for controlled tests.

Do not use invented admission requirements as test fixtures for claiming that real programmes are eligible.

